            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain, enzymes and hypothyroidism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>168-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hypothyroidism is a common disorder and when presenting with classical symptoms and signs is easy to recognise. However, hypothyroidism may present in a manner suggestive of an acute myocardial infarction with an elevated creatine kinase and electrocardiographic abnormalities. We report a case of severe hypothyroidism presenting as a cardiac event whose symptoms and signs dispersed following treatment with thyroxine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
